\f0\b\fs22 \cf0 \cb2 The Hy The Man - The story\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl260\ql\qnatural

\b0 \cf0 \cb1 Let me tell you a story....\
\
I once outpaced a Pegasus on a stars strucked night. The wind or should I say the breeze was mighty refreshing and the hills showered in all its beauty. The Pegasus named Al el Faxizi by the great emperor of the northern hemisphere never thought anything about my chances to claim the crown for this race. Many races had been completed with a ridicules amount of wins for this fine example of a Pegasus. To be fair, the opinion was not on my behalf if I should say. That could never hobble my curiosity for speed and the many ways of producing it when needed. So!! The card was on the table. I on one side spiked on adrenalin, longing for the show that this magnificent race was out to be. On the other side: Al el Faxizi - The greatest Pegasus ever walk on this side of Tellus since his father died. His genes, moulded by thousand generations of higher sensed creatures.\
Could I touch him? One on one battle was my art form. I had many victories in countries far away from this. This was his territory, with the all the benefits of being raised on these fine surroundings. I was not one who runs when the hot steam caused others to fail their missions. Even so, I admit that this would be the sign, could I win and earn the sought after name - The Hy The Man. I fancy my chances.\
\
A stream of chillness went thru my bones, I saw him lurking, and the moon flattered the corner of his eye. He for once was not totally satisfied with the challenger this time; I posed a severe threat to his position.\
We adjust to starting positions. Not yet had the old bell fine sound reached the field. It was an ancient way of ringing a delayed song, which is used for this kind of races. First the vibration comes; smooth to say the least, then! A muffled sound, almost intimidated by it's own sheer power but never so long that it missed the set time for the race to begin. Off we go!\
Do I need to say more, if you look at the name I use as a headline.\
I will reveal for you that it wasn't a straight forward victory, once we side by side saw the touchline that was made out to be the end I arouse in a as was written later on in the pulsated news around the world. The bulletin said "Never in history anything could have matched this invoke of force to push him self to this celebrated key victory. He must have seen visions that for us everyday living beings, only would come an inch closer to touch when we trying the most. To overcome Al el Faxizi, it was a success. Also with the posture and grace he produced the word after I quote " I won't dwell on this honour for to long thou more things are set out for me, I thank everyone who done there work splendid and wish Al el Faxizi a great life, I hope the judgment upon him is not sent in a wrong way. I hold him at the highest regards. Merci avec beaucoup de coeur!}